unless I give everything I've got.</i>

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:13.420
<i>But...</i>

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:18.380
<b>Win th{*\c&H3F3C45&\3c&HC3C7CC&}e {*\c&H353334&\3c&HAFA0A3&}A{*\c&H2C2724&\3c&HAE9F9E&}r{*\c&H322B25&\3c&HAC9791&}i{*\c&H322B28&\3c&HAE9895&}m{*\c&H3C3B38&\3c&HAA8E88&}a {*\c&H343230&\3c&HAF8E86&}K{*\c&H302E2C&\3c&HA88681&}i{*\c&H2D2A27&\3c&HA07D7F&}n{*\c&H292623&\3c&HA5857B&}e{*\c&H25211F&\3c&HA4847C&}n{*\c&H221D1A&\3c&H9F7D75&}!!</b>

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:15.830
I want to win!

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:21.130
It's that time once again.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:23.590
As the new year draws closer, 
here at the Nakayama Racecourse,

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:25.600
a simmering intensity from 
the crowds and the track is

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.510
enough to push back the seasonal cold.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:29.100
It's time for the G1 Arima Kinen!

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.490
It certainly is. And with such 
a remarkable lineup this year,

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:33.310
I think we're looking at an amazing race.

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:38.950
Every year, the horse girls invited to run 
in this race are chosen by fan ballot.

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:38.680
There's always something 
in the air during Arima...

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:41.700
It really does feel like 
the year is wrapping up.

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:42.860
And this year, we have eight remarkable 
contenders vying for this G1 title!

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:42.860
Good point.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:46.370
<i>There's no doubt in my mind that this will 
be a fitting race to conclude the year!</i>

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:47.990
<b>Arima Kinen</b>

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:49.280
<i>Who do you see winning this, Hosoe-san?</i>

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:51.180
<i>I'm inclined to think it'll be
 a competitor from BNW</i>

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:52.660
<i>who's here to represent 
the next generation.</i>

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:54.920
<i>I think we can also look forward 
to seeing Mejiro Palmer</i>

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:58.020
<i>continue her outrunning spree early on.</i>

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:01.760
<i>Thanks for the input. Will we see a changing 
of the guard at this year's Arima Kinen?</i>

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.010
The horse girls will soon 
be taking to the track.

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:18.050
Teio! You got a second?

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:19.660
Oh, what's up?

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.280
Prez?

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.280
Thank you, Trainer.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:23.950
Don't mention it.

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:30.060
You haven't worn that since the derby.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:32.960
Yeah. I wanted to run in this today.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:33.860
I see.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:41.160
Listen, can I ask you something weird?

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:47.340
Did you ever do anything special when 
you wanted to win, no matter what?

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:52.950
That's a tough one.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:57.570
Everyone who enters a race wants to win it.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:00.610
They've built themselves 
up in pursuit of victory...

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:04.710
Gaining strength, focusing, 
all of it aimed toward competition.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:10.910
But in spite of that, no matter 
how good your condition is,

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:12.720
there's always room for surprises.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:14.320
Anything can happen in a race.

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:16.580
That said...

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:22.130
If you have something you believe in, 
something that you will never yield on...

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.990
That's one thing no one else can affect.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:30.520
Did that help at all?

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:33.640
<b>T{*\c&H79726C&\3c&HE1D9D5&}o{*\c&H7F7974&}k{*\c&H86807B&\3c&HE0DAD6&}a{*\c&H8D8782&}i {*\c&H9A9691&\3c&HE0DAD7&}T{*\c&HA19D98&\3c&HDFDBD8&}e{*\c&HA7A4A0&}io</b>

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:32.940
Yeah! Thanks, Prez.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:37.640
The horse girls are taking to 
the turf one after another.

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:42.070
Is she a heel, or is she a hero? 
It's the blessing star, Rice Shower.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:43.950
She put on an amazing display when she upset

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:46.070
Mejiro McQueen to take the Fall Tennoushou.

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:50.250
I'm looking forward to the performance
 such a standout stayer puts on for us.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:55.080
And here we have the winner of last 
year's Arima Kinen, Mejiro Palmer!

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:58.150
She's a first-rate outrunner horse girl.

00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:00.830
If she takes the lead early 
on and sets the pace,

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:02.400
we could be looking at a consecutive win.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:05.030
Then there's Machikane Tannhäuser,

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:07.650
who cuts an imposing figure when 
it comes to long distance races.

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:10.250
Nice Nature will also be looking 
to relinquish her title of

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:12.220
"Bronze Collector" to win this year's Arima.

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:14.590
Nature-san seems to be in good shape.

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:15.410
Right.

00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:17.680
I hope Tannhäuser-san can use the 
frustration over her last race

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:19.400
to accomplish something this time around.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.520
I wanted to run in this!

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.770
You should take that enthusiasm 
and put it into your cheering.

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.860
Hey, is there any chance 
I could join in still?!

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.170
No, there isn't.

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:28.450
Fine...

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:32.320
At the Japan Cup, she managed to outdo 
famous competitors from around the globe,

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:34.800
scoring Relic Earth a significant victory.

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:38.940
And across from her is one of the symbols 
of the next generation, Winning Ticket.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:41.570
All you need to say is that she's 
this year's Derby horse girl.

00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:43.250
I'm going to be paying attention to see

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:44.890
if she lives up to those expectations.

00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:46.010
A good point.

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:50.870
And here's Tokai Teio, returning to 
the turf after a year-long absence.

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:54.640
Despite the long hiatus, she's the fourth 
most popular contender in the Arima Kinen!

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:57.630
A lot of people have been 
waiting for her return.

00:06:57.630 --> 00:07:01.020
You can tell how strong the support 
for her is with that high ranking.

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:03.030
Everybody looks so strong...

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:04.630
You can't get intimidated, Kita-chan!

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:07.710
Teio-san has to do a good job 
for McQueen-san's take, too!

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:08.890
Y-You're right.

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:12.990
And here we have today's 
star runner, Biwa Hayahide.

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:15.660
One hundred percent of her races have 
had her in the top two!

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:19.620
The undisputed most popular racer! Will she 
be able to live up to the fans' expectations?

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:22.840
She's shown even greater 
development since summer.

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:26.010
I think anyone looking to beat 
her will have their hands full.

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:29.860
I'm back.

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:31.440
Teio...

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:33.800
Nature?

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:36.160
I don't know what kind 
of condition you're in,

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:38.520
and I don't care how you're going to run.

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:43.150
All I care about is clearing the goal 
before you, and before anyone else.

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:46.310
Yeah. I'm not losing to anyone else, either.

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:48.720
Let's make this a good race.

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:51.030
Oh, and...

00:07:51.890 --> 00:07:53.800
Welcome back, Teio.

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:57.000
It's good to be back.

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:05.360
<i>You're out there watching, right?</i>

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:09.920
<b>Umamusume</b>

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:09.920
<b><i>Pretty Derby</i></b>

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:21.370
<i>I'm frightened.</i>

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:24.430
<i>Too frightened to watch...</i>

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:27.990
<i>I want to believe in Teio.</i>

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:33.290
<i>But... if she were to lose, I'd...</i>

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:40.200
The fanfare is now echoing 
throughout the stands.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.940
The Arima Kinen determines 
who ends the year on top...

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:45.770
And the horse girls are 
entering their brackets.

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:49.770
Each one of them is solemnly focused 
on living up to their fans' hopes,

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:52.210
waiting for the moment that the gate opens.

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:55.220
And on the far side gate, 
Mejiro Palmer is now in position.

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:58.060
All fourteen competitors 
are now in their brackets.

00:08:58.060 --> 00:09:00.220
It's the last G1 race of the year,
the Arima Kinen!

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:02.400
And they're off!

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:05.230
Mejiro Palmer is out in front,
 with a good start!

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:07.510
These horse girls all seem 
to have made a smooth start!

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:10.250
You can see why these fourteen were selected!
 A fine group of competitors!

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:12.010
Teio's running...

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:12.730
Yeah.

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:13.840
Teio...

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:15.360
I'm glad I got to see this.

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:17.970
Who from BNW is gonna win today?

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:19.370
Probably Biwa Hayahide.

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:24.480
The last time Tokai Teio raced 
was last year's Arima Kinen...

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:27.930
It's been 364 days since then. 
Her return came after a long blank.

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:28.750
What's brought that on?

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:31.600
There's never been a single horse girl

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:33.260
that has won a G1 race 
after such a long hiatus!

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:34.550
Do you think she can pull it off?

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:37.370
You're really gonna ask that? 
She came in 11th last year.

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:38.170
My bad.

00:09:38.170 --> 00:09:40.010
Of course it'll be hard!

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:42.390
But Teio-san's still running!

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:43.970
She's right!

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:44.920
Yep.

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:51.070
<i>There really is nothing like a real race!</i>

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:54.190
<i>I can feel them around me... 
feel how much they want to win...</i>

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:56.130
<i>I can sense all kinds of stuff!</i>

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:58.760
<i>I wanted to get a bigger lead, 
but they're right on my tail!</i>

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:01.160
<i>But my legs are still good to go!</i>

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:04.180
<i>I might've given up the Kikkashou, 
but this time I'm winning!</i>

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:06.920
<i>I'll win this race, 
and win cheers and adulation!</i>

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:08.020
<i>I don't wanna lose!</i>

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:11.670
<i>I have to cross the goal in first place, 
not second, and definitely not third!</i>

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:14.170
<i>I can be the star, too!</i>

00:10:14.590 --> 00:10:16.700
Coming around the fourth corner,
they're in front of the stands.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:19.550
<i>But... I can't lose! I won't lose!</i>

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:19.550
These fourteen elite racers are bathed 
in cheers as they make their way onward.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:21.450
<i>Mejiro Palmer is still in the lead.</i>

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:23.110
<i>Biwa Hayahide is currently in fourth place,</i>

00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:24.840
<i>with Rice Shower moving up on the outside.</i>

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:27.320
<i>Tokai Teio seems to be a 
bit further to the back.</i>

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:30.310
<i>One has to wonder how she's feeling, 
running after an entire year.</i>

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:29.280
Teio...

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:32.810
Come on! You can do this, Teio!

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:34.490
I wonder how she's doing?

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:37.160
She tended to drift a little 
to the right during practice.

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:39.670
You saw how much she trained! She'll be fine!

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:42.570
She didn't manage to get back to 
where she used to be in time.

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:48.510
But we'll still be cheering for 
you until the very end, Teio!

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:51.900
The horse girls are now entering 
the home stretch of the first lap.

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:55.710
<i>The chosen 14 are running in front 
of the entire Nakayama crowd.</i>

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:55.710
Tokai Teio-san...

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:57.710
Tokai Teio can't win?!

00:10:57.930 --> 00:11:01.840
The hell are you saying, boss?! 
Look at how hard she's trying!

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:04.090
Anybody can try hard.

00:11:04.090 --> 00:11:06.670
If that's all it took to win, life'd be easy.

00:11:06.670 --> 00:11:10.480
If Teio pulls this off, I'll shave my head.

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:13.980
<i>The 14 racers are now coming around the 
second corner and entering the backstretch!</i>

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:16.480
Let's check their position.

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:20.490
Mejiro Palmer in the lead, with Vice Stone 
in second, and Relic Earth in third.

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:24.620
Biwa Hayahide is in fourth, and behind 
her are Winning Ticket and Rice Shower.

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:27.060
The returning Tokai Teio followed by Pella,

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:31.040
Ferment Win, Nice Nature, 
Duo Priwen, Spur Mover,

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:35.000
Avec Dream, and Machikane 
Tannhäuser at the moment!

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:39.950
<i>As expected, the early lead is going 
to the Mejiro clan's star outrunner,</i>

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:41.380
<i>Mejiro Palmer.</i>

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:46.010
That's true. But this year, all thirteen 
of her competitors are within ten lengths.

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:50.020
There's still no telling who 
could move up in position.

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:53.060
So watch me, McQueen.

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:56.650
<i>She managed to outrun the competition to 
the end during last year's Arima Kinen.</i>

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:58.680
It's now a question of who's 
going to take action,

00:11:58.680 --> 00:12:00.860
as they begin to enter the third corner.

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:02.280
<i>I'm gonna win!</i>

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:03.660
<i>I'm going to win!</i>

00:12:03.650 --> 00:12:04.910
<i>I'm gonna win!</i>

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:06.160
<i>I'm gonna win!</i>

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:07.660
<i>I'm gonna win!</i>

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:11.160
<i>I have to... I have to!</i>

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:13.690
The racers are making their 
way into the fourth corner.

00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:16.730
Biwa Hayahide and Winning Ticket 
are steadily moving up...

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:18.420
Is Relic Earth making her move?

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:21.880
Whoa! And it looks like Biwa 
Hayahide is taking off!

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:25.680
The winner of the Kikkashou, Biwa Hayahide, 
is making her way forward in the ranks!

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:29.650
Mejiro Palmer is passed! Biwa Hayahide 
is now in the lead! She's in first!

00:12:29.650 --> 00:12:32.170
Biwa Hayahide is strong enough 
to justify her popularity!

00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:34.900
Is there any horse girl here 
who can keep up with her?!

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:37.320
Will it be Rice Shower? Nice Nature?

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:39.050
What about Winning Ticket?!

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:40.780
<i>You're not getting away from me!</i>

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:16.960
Tokai Teio is closing in!

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:19.400
Wait... Tokai Teio is closing in?!

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:00.650
<i>My lungs hurt.</i>

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:02.650
<i>But I don't care if they burst!</i>

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:06.360
<i>My legs are so heavy. 
But they're still moving!</i>

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:10.200
<i>I lost my way so many times!</i>

00:14:10.900 --> 00:14:13.200
<i>Back then... And then...</i>

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:15.700
<i>More than anyone else!</i>

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:19.200
<i>I've felt frustrated more than anyone else!</i>

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:22.860
<i>And I want to win more than anyone else!</i>

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:28.960
<i>So I'm not letting you win! 
No matter what... No matter what!</i>

00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:33.700
<i>No matter what, I'm winning!</i>

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:40.480
Go...

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:41.480
Go!

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:43.980
Go! Run!

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:47.640
Let's do this!

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:50.940
It's Tokai Teio! Tokai Teio is moving up!

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:53.060
She's closing in on Biwa Hayahide's lead!

00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:56.490
There's 200 meters left! Tokai Teio 
hasn't been on the track in a year!

00:14:56.710 --> 00:14:59.000
Will she be able to catch 
up to Biwa Hayahide?!

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:01.380
She's giving everything she has to move up!

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:04.200
Teio-san!

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:05.330
Teio!

00:15:05.740 --> 00:15:08.760
Tokai Teio chases! 
But Biwa Hayahide won't be caught!

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:09.690
<i>One length between them!</i>

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:10.010
Go!

00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:12.760
But that last gap doesn't seem 
to shrink for Tokai Teio!

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:14.700
Biwa Hayahide isn't budging!

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:17.360
She's demonstrating the strength 
that set a <i>record at the Kikkashou!</i>

00:15:16.510 --> 00:15:17.770
Go!

00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:18.890
<i>She won't let Tokai Teio pass!</i>

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:18.890
Go for it!

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:20.890
But Tokai Teio is still closing in!

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:22.400
Go!

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:24.410
<i>Having returned to the track, 
</i>Teio slowly crosses the gap!

00:15:24.410 --> 00:15:27.260
There's 100 meters in the race!
 Only 100 meters to go!

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:25.900
Go!

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:26.900
Go!

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:29.400
Go... Go!

00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:30.650
This is the last battle! Will Tokai Teio 
be able to catch up to Biwa Hayahide?!

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:34.250
Will it be the symbol of the new generation, 
Biwa Hayahide, or the revived Tokai Teio?!

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:36.910
Nakayama... Nakayama is 
shaking for the Arima Kinen!

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:38.910
Which of these two will seize victory?!

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:47.110
It's Tokai Teio! Tokai Teio passes her!

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:48.890
Tokai Teio takes a slight lead!

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:49.920
Go!

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:52.090
But it's a narrow one! <i>Biwa Hayahide 
will be looking to catch up!</i>

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:51.300
Go!

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:52.680
Go!

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:54.180
<i>Is it going to be Tokai Teio
 or Biwa Hayahide?!</i>

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:54.180
Go!

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:57.680
Tokai Teio and Biwa Hayahide! 
Tokai Teio! Biwa Hayahide!

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:00.180
Will the Derby winner hold strong?!

00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:03.710
Tokai Teio! Tokai Teio is in the lead!

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:07.380
Tokai Teio makes a miraculous return!

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:16.690
I did it.

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:21.800
After an entire year...

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:24.970
Tokai Teio has managed to win 
this race. It's a miracle.

00:16:24.970 --> 00:16:29.120
She has demonstrated nothing 
less than a miracle on this day!

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:31.280
Who could have imagined it?!

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:36.090
For the first time since last year's 
Arima Kinen, Tokai Teio has raced...

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:38.100
And she has managed to defeat 
thirteen other challengers!

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:41.100
<i>Hosoe-san, this has been a huge shock!</i>

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:41.100
<b>Arima Kinen</b>

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:43.890
<i>I can't believe what I just saw. 
We're looking at a historic moment.</i>

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:45.100
<i>I have to agree.</i>

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:47.950
<i>Winning a G1 race after such 
a significant hiatus...</i>

00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:50.650
<i>It's something that's never been done before!</i>

00:16:50.650 --> 00:16:53.970
<i>Three fractures </i>left doubt 
if she'd ever run again,

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:56.360
and after being told she was done for,

00:16:56.360 --> 00:17:01.070
Tokai Teio has grasped a historic 
victory through an indomitable spirit!

00:17:01.070 --> 00:17:02.960
It was truly a remarkable win,

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:06.050
against an incredible G1 lineup, 
after such a long time.

00:17:06.050 --> 00:17:09.480
This was a race that defied the 
expectations of the Twinkle Series.

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:13.090
Biwa Hayahide seemed to have things wrapped 
up entering the final straightaway,

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:17.730
but Tokai Teio's almost obsessive acceleration 
forced her into second place.

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:21.810
<b>Nakayama</b>

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:21.810
<b>Results</b>

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:21.810
<b>Turf: Good
Time:</b>

00:17:17.730 --> 00:17:20.530
There was a lineup of horse girls today 
where any one of them could have won,

00:17:20.530 --> 00:17:24.010
but in the end, Tokai Teio's dedication 
is what let her come out on top.

00:17:24.010 --> 00:17:25.900
Nice Nature put on an admirable performance,

00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:48.120
Teio! Teio! Teio! {repeat as necssary}

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:28.480
but will sadly have to settle 
for third place again this year.

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:31.820
Oh, and there's a Teio chant!

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:34.350
The same one heard on the 
day of the Japan Derby!

00:17:34.350 --> 00:17:37.360
No, I think it might be even louder!

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:39.660
It echoes throughout the Nakayama Racecourse!

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:42.320
Tokai Teio has dazzled 
all of these fans today!

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:46.580
Overturning all expectations and casting 
the very notion of submission aside,

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:51.520
she has given rise to a new 
legend in the Arima Kinen!

00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:49.750
Teio...

00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:52.630
Teio might have just outdone the Emperor!

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:55.260
I guess prodigies really do exist, 
as frustrating as that might be!

00:17:52.630 --> 00:18:11.000
Teio! Teio! Teio! {repeat as necssary}

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:57.280
Thanks, guys.

00:17:57.280 --> 00:17:59.680
You... holy... Tei...

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:01.720
We can't even tell what you're saying!

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:03.080
You did it, Teio!

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:06.030
Teio-san, congratulations!

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:08.850
Suzuka-san is happy, too!

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:10.170
Yeah. Thanks.

00:18:10.170 --> 00:18:11.650
Huh? She's not answering?

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:13.730
It really was a wonderful race.

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:15.900
Congratulations, Teio.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:17.750
Suzuka-san?! Why?!

00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:20.400
I wanted to cheer her on 
in person, so I flew in.

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:22.660
Suzuka-san!

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:25.810
You should've told me you were coming!

00:18:30.320 --> 00:18:31.460
Did you see that?

00:18:31.950 --> 00:18:34.490
Yes... I did.

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:38.800
Thank you, Teio!

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:40.430
McQueen—

00:18:43.050 --> 00:18:45.480
What!? What is all this?!

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:48.560
Hey, you guys are kinda heavy!

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:52.960
Congratulations, Teio!

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:54.330
Congratulations!

00:18:55.940 --> 00:18:57.680
Congratulations.

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:00.120
Thanks, Rice.

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:21.150
<i>I wanna run to a dream with you,</i>

00:19:21.150 --> 00:19:28.520
<i>over and over, until we see 
what's beyond victory!</i>

00:19:38.670 --> 00:19:41.240
<i>We're young, so let's have a good time</i>

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:46.870
<i>No matter how tough it gets, if you enjoy yourself,
 the crowds will cheer you on!</i>

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:48.660
<i>Full points for spirit!</i>

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:53.350
<i>I think if I was on my own, 
I never would've realized</i>

00:19:53.350 --> 00:19:57.540
<i>There's no room for "impossible" 
in my dictionary!</i>

00:19:57.540 --> 00:19:59.880
<i>Just like a puzzle,</i>

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:03.260
<i>you have the future, now, and yesterday!</i>

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:04.210
<i>No more!</i>

00:20:04.210 --> 00:20:06.000
<i>Not gonna lose our way!</i>

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:06.720
<i>Let's go!</i>

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:09.140
<i>And we're never gonna stop!</i>

00:20:09.380 --> 00:20:11.730
<i>I wanna run to a dream with you,</i>

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:14.500
<i>pushing each other to always get better!</i>

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:16.310
<i>With endless power, I can be!</i>

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:20.150
<i>And even if I fall, I'll get up once again!</i>

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:22.480
<i>Try! Always at full power!</i>

00:20:22.480 --> 00:20:25.410
<i>The future all depends on you!</i>

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:27.530
<i>We'll zip right past expectations</i>

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:33.710
<i>Leaving them behind and making 
an unforgettable miracle real!</i>

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:34.330
<i>Come on!</i>

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:36.080
<i>We're sharing the same dream!</i>

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:36.780
<i>Come on!</i>

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:38.650
<i>The sun is high in my heart!</i>

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:40.050
<i>And you better never forget!</i>

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:42.300
<i>I wanna run to a dream with you,</i>

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:46.360
<i>where our hopes will always be waiting!</i>

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:52.280
<i>I'll be up there one day.</i>

00:21:08.270 --> 00:21:11.740
This is why I told you to go to 
bed early before important days!

00:21:11.740 --> 00:21:15.500
I mean, come on! I was too 
nervous to sleep, anyway!

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:18.500
<b>Entrance Ceremony</b>

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:22.510
<b>Entrance
Ceremony</b>

00:21:26.990 --> 00:21:28.950
We're finally here, Dia-chan.

00:21:28.950 --> 00:21:31.480
Yeah. Let's work hard together, Kita-chan.

00:21:40.370 --> 00:21:41.940
I apologize for the wait.

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:48.600
Nah. No apologies necessary.

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:51.250
We can finally race each other.

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:52.460
Yes.

00:21:53.780 --> 00:21:58.820
Two thousand and four hundred meters on turf.
 Clear weather. Track condition, good.

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:02.050
Just don't cry if you lose, okay?

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:04.800
You're up against the strongest 
horse girl, after all.

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:06.920
I wouldn't have it any other way.
